# XSH bsearch()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Which of several equal members is returned is unspecified; the tests only
# require a member that compares equal.

assertion  XSH.bsearch.001
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       For sorted arrays of distinct ints of 1, 2, 3, 10 and 257
           elements, bsearch() with each element's value as key returns a
           pointer to that element.
test       t/001-found.c

assertion  XSH.bsearch.002
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       A key below the first, above the last or between two elements,
           and any key in a one-element array that does not match, gives a
           null pointer.
test       t/002-not-found.c

assertion  XSH.bsearch.003
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With nel zero the comparison function is not called and the
           result is a null pointer.
test       t/003-empty.c

assertion  XSH.bsearch.004
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Every call to the comparison function has the key's address as
           its first argument and, as its second, the address of an array
           element (an element boundary inside the array, for records
           7 bytes wide); a non-empty search makes at least one call, and a
           negative result moves the search toward lower elements and a
           positive one toward higher elements (every record is found).
test       t/004-compar-args.c

assertion  XSH.bsearch.005
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/bsearch.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       When several members compare equal to the key, bsearch() returns
           a pointer to one of them, and the contents of the array are
           unchanged afterwards.
test       t/005-duplicates.c
